From 8fd793b8511ec840c1d43552313bf0d74dc96483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 12:18:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(onboarding): UX & consent fixes for MonoOnboarding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes #105

- Consent: only persist a live-sharing decision when the user actually
  interacts with the checkbox (track consentTouched); never pre-write
  "declined" for an untouched control. Fix the stale "public-by-default"
  comment to reflect the opt-in default.
- Username availability: persistent aria-live="polite" status region with a
  non-color valence glyph (✓/✕/⚠); add a watchdog timeout state so a stuck
  pending check surfaces an actionable message instead of an endless spinner;
  set aria-invalid on the input for error/taken/timeout.
- "Skip for now" -> "Skip & finish": clearer label, disabled while submitting,
  plus an explanatory line that sports are optional.
- Move focus to each step's heading on step change (tabIndex={-1}); remove
  input/heading autofocus races.
- Enlarge nav/back/skip/checkbox touch targets to >=44px.
- OAuth name pre-fill: fix effect deps ([clerkUser, firstName, lastName,
  onChange]) with an empty-guard so the Google name is no longer missed.
- Skip step 1 (Name) once when Clerk already has a name, prefilling state.

Adds MonoOnboarding.test.jsx covering focus movement, skip-step-1 + payload
carry-through, aria-live availability/timeout, 3-way consent persistence, and
the 44px Back target.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
